  <section>
    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>Founding Farmers is the only dispensary currently operating in the town of Limerick, Maine. Established in 2021, the store sits on Main Street in central Limerick and serves as a regional access point for medical patients and adult-use customers across the rural western York County corridor — including Limington, Parsonsfield, Hiram, Cornish, Newfield, and Shapleigh.</p>
    <p>The store's public menu spans the full cannabis product range: flower, edibles, extracts, pre-rolls, vapes, topicals, drinks, and glassware accessories. Founding Farmers advertises both in-store pickup and delivery through its own website and third-party platforms.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Location, Hours, and Access</h2>
    <p><strong>Address:</strong> 16 Main Street, Limerick, ME 04048<br>
    <strong>Phone:</strong> (207) 315-5259<br>
    <strong>Hours (per operator website, July 2026):</strong> Sunday through Wednesday 11AM to 7PM; Thursday through Saturday 10AM to 8PM.</p>
    <p>Limerick is a small town of roughly 3,200 residents in York County, located about 35 miles west of Portland and 18 miles east of Bridgton. The store's central Main Street location makes it accessible from the surrounding rural communities, several of which do not have their own dispensaries. Visitors from the Bridgton and Fryeburg areas find Founding Farmers a reasonable drive via Route 5 / Route 11.</p>
    <p>Founding Farmers operates primarily out of a single storefront; there is no second Maine location at the time of this writing. If a second location opens, it will most likely be referenced first on the operator's official site.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Product Menu</h2>
    <p>Founding Farmers carries a full Maine dispensary menu organized into eight categories on their public site:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Flower</strong> — fresh whole-bud cannabis in multiple cultivars</li>
      <li><strong>Edibles</strong> — gummies, chocolates, and other infused products</li>
      <li><strong>Extracts / Concentrates</strong> — solvent and solventless options</li>
      <li><strong>Pre-rolls</strong> — single joints and multi-packs</li>
      <li><strong>Vapes / Cartridges</strong> — 510-thread carts and all-in-one disposables</li>
      <li><strong>Topicals / Tinctures</strong> — non-inhalable formats</li>
      <li><strong>Drinks</strong> — cannabis-infused beverages</li>
      <li><strong>Glass</strong> — pipes, rigs, and accessories</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The operator's site highlights brands including Method Maine flower (marketed as "Mineral salts combined with organic inputs, pesticide and mold free") and Kind Farms edibles, among others. Live menu and pricing should be confirmed directly with the operator before visiting, as inventory rotates.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Pickup and Delivery</h2>
    <p>Founding Farmers offers both in-store pickup and delivery. Pickup orders can be placed through the operator's website (ffmaine.com) or via Weedmaps. Delivery availability and radius should be confirmed by phone — delivery rules in Maine are license-category-specific and may vary based on whether the customer is a registered medical patient or an adult-use customer.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>York County Service Area</h2>
    <p>Founding Farmers is the nearest dispensary for several small western York County towns that have no local options of their own. A non-exhaustive list of communities the store serves:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Limerick</strong> (in town)</li>
      <li><strong>Limington</strong> — ~6 miles east, no dispensary</li>
      <li><strong>Parsonsfield</strong> — ~7 miles west, no dispensary</li>
      <li><strong>Hiram</strong> — ~10 miles north, no dispensary</li>
      <li><strong>Cornish</strong> — ~10 miles northeast, no dispensary</li>
      <li><strong>Newfield</strong> — ~10 miles southwest, no dispensary</li>
      <li><strong>Shapleigh</strong> — ~10 miles south, no dispensary</li>
      <li><strong>Waterboro / Lyman</strong> — 12–15 miles southeast</li>
    </ul>
    <p>For adult-use customers closer to Portland, Biddeford, Saco, or Old Orchard Beach, additional dispensaries exist in those larger commercial centers. For adult-use customers further west, Bridgton and Fryeburg dispensaries are closer.</p>
  </section>

